{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08FH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$j : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}/U), \\mathcal{O}_U) \\to (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0005": "$j^*$", "MATH_0006": "$Lj^*$", "MATH_0007": "$$\nD(\\mathcal{O}) \\to D(\\mathcal{O}_U),\n\\quad\nE \\mapsto j^*E = E|_U\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$j_! : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_U) \\to \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0009": "$$\nj_! : D(\\mathcal{O}_U) \\to D(\\mathcal{O}), \\quad\nF \\mapsto j_!F\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$j_!$", "MATH_0011": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-definition-localize-ringed-site}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-extension-by-zero-exact}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d3b4edf2fe4a695102f41edcbf9345e1be97aad589b66e046540845975f90123", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:588ae5465fad17e2b10a256596d5f2278b563f01f8ad6d27ff8b9215b5d22e1c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a ringed site. Let <MATH_0002> be an\nobject of <MATH_0003>. Denote\n<MATH_0004>\nthe corresponding localization morphism. The pullback functor <MATH_0005> is exact\nas it is just the restriction functor. Thus derived pullback <MATH_0006> is\ncomputed on any complex by simply restricting the complex. We often\nsimply denote the corresponding functor\n<MATH_0007>\nSimilarly, extension by zero\n<MATH_0008> (see\nModules on Sites, Definition\n<REF_0001>)\nis an exact functor\n(Modules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nThus it induces a functor\n<MATH_0009>\nby simply applying <MATH_0010> to any complex representing the object <MATH_0011>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa2c6e2659e47b82b11b77346fe57902ca4178c7a591533cd433db57db980b26", "unit_id": "tag: